From eec43842f296fa2b755169affbede6469f627817 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:09:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix deadlock when a script ends while stop() raises
 SystemExit

CPythonInvoker::stop() raises SystemExit in a script that didn't stop in
5 seconds. It released m_critical to take the GIL, then took m_critical
back while holding the GIL, but onExecutionDone() takes m_critical first
and then the GIL. A script that ended just as stop() gave up waiting for
it could leave the two waiting for each other. stop() runs with
CScriptInvocationManager's lock held, so the main thread then blocks in
CScriptInvocationManager::Process() and Kodi's GUI freezes. Disabling an
add-on whose service is just ending is enough to get there.

stop() no longer takes m_critical back. Without it, onExecutionDone()
could end the script's interpreter while stop() is still waiting for the
GIL with a thread state of that interpreter, which ending it frees on
Python 3.14. So stop() counts its thread state while it exists, and
onExecutionDone() waits for the count to drop before it ends the
interpreter, then drops a SystemExit queued for its own thread, as the
script has already ended.

Assisted-by: Claude
